  {"question": "Can Muse access Messages and Notes on my Mac?", "answer": "Yes, through Muse for Mac after system authorization. Review macOS permissions and each app\u2019s Off, Read only, or Read and interact setting."},
  {"question": "Are Facebook, Instagram, and Threads connected automatically?", "answer": "Yes, when those accounts are in the same Accounts Center. Review account connections and permissions before assigning tasks."},
  {"question": "Can I chat with Muse in WhatsApp?", "answer": "Yes. Meta lists WhatsApp as a Muse chat entry point where available."},

  {
    question: 'What do I need before setting up Meta Muse?',
    answer:
      'You need a Meta account, the web version, an iOS or Android phone, or the Mac app, and a Google account if you plan to connect Gmail or Google Calendar. Access varies by location and account.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I have to pay to use Meta Muse?',
    answer:
      'No. Meta Muse has a free tier with a usage limit. Power costs $20/month with 500M Muse tokens/week; Maximum costs $100/month with 3B/week. Additional tokens can also be purchased.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Meta Muse access my email and calendar?',
    answer:
      'Gmail and Google Calendar require connection; Meta accounts in the same Accounts Center can connect automatically. Grant access only when a task needs it, review permission settings, and approve sensitive actions. You can disconnect a service later.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What can Meta Muse not do?',
    answer:
      'The cloud browser runs in a separate virtual machine. Tasks depend on available websites, Connectors, permissions, and account access. Access varies by region and account, and desktop capabilities depend on the client you use.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Where does Meta Muse run my tasks?',
    answer:
      'Cloud browsing runs in Muse Secure VM. The Mac app can additionally access local files and apps after macOS authorization; cloud isolation does not remove those local permissions.',
  },
